# Exam track — Theme: Sproochen — Sub-lesson 1: Vocabulary
# Sproochentest oral-exam topic. Target level ~B1 (authoring guideline only).
#
# Sentences are grounded in the user's real answers, gathered by interview —
# do not "improve" or genericize them in a later editing pass.
#
# Handout corrections applied after LOD verification: Preposition ->
# Prepositioun, Italienesch -> Italieenesch, Kolleg -> Kolleeg,
# Liiblingswuert -> Liblingswuert.

@lesson L1.01 "Language Vocabulary"

@word d'Sprooch = the language
@word d'Mammesprooch = the mother tongue
@word d'Friemsprooch = the foreign language
@word de Wuertschatz = the vocabulary
@word d'Grammatik = the grammar
@word d'Aussprooch = the pronunciation
@word de Saz = the sentence
@word d'Wuert = the word
@word de Feeler = the mistake
@word den Dialekt = the dialect
@word d'Iwwersetzung = the translation
@word den Iwwersetzer = the translator
@word den Ufänger = the beginner
@word de Mammesproochler = the native speaker
@word d'Sproocheschoul = the language school
@word de Cours = the course
@word d'Reegel = the rule
@word d'Übung = the exercise
@word de Dativ = the dative
@word d'Prepositiounen = the prepositions
@word d'Vokabelen = the vocables
@word d'Karteikaarten = the index cards
@word d'App = the app
@word d'Wierderbuch = the dictionary
@word de Noutfall = the emergency
@word de Niveau = the level
@word de Fortschrëtt = the progress
@word d'Gedold = the patience
@word d'Motivatioun = the motivation
@word d'Disziplin = the discipline
@word d'Kommunikatioun = the communication
@word Lëtzebuergesch = Luxembourgish
@word Ukrainesch = Ukrainian
@word Englesch = English
@word Franséisch = French
@word Italieenesch = Italian
@word Russesch = Russian
@word schwätzen = to speak
@word léieren = to learn
@word verstoen = to understand
@word lauschteren = to listen
@word liesen = to read
@word schreiwen = to write
@word iwwersetzen = to translate
@word erklären = to explain
@word widderhuelen = to repeat
@word benotzen = to use
@word üben = to practise
@word kommunizéieren = to communicate
@word vergiessen = to forget
@word notéieren = to note down
@word fléissend = fluent
@word nëtzlech = useful
@word praktesch = practical
@word exakt = accurate
@word spannend = exciting
@word komplizéiert = complicated

@sentence
@lu Meng Mammesprooch ass Ukrainesch.
@en My mother tongue is Ukrainian.
@distractor-lu Franséisch
@distractor-lu Dialekt
@distractor-en French
@distractor-en dialect

@sentence
@lu Ech léiere Lëtzebuergesch säit bal engem Joer.
@en I have been learning Luxembourgish for almost a year.
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu Woch
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en week

@sentence
@lu D'Grammatik ass fir mech méi schwéier wéi de Wuertschatz.
@en The grammar is more difficult for me than the vocabulary.
@distractor-lu Aussprooch
@distractor-lu einfach
@distractor-en pronunciation
@distractor-en easy

@sentence
@lu Ech maache Feeler mam Dativ a mat de Prepositiounen.
@en I make mistakes with the dative and with the prepositions.
@distractor-lu Wuert
@distractor-lu Aussprooch
@distractor-en word
@distractor-en pronunciation

@sentence
@lu Ech benotzen eng App an heiansdo Karteikaarten.
@en I use an app and sometimes index cards.
@distractor-lu Wierderbuch
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en dictionary
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@lu Ech schwätze gär mat Mammesproochler.
@en I like speaking with native speakers.
@distractor-lu Ufänger
@distractor-lu schreiwen
@distractor-en beginners
@distractor-en write

@sentence
@lu Et brauch ee vill Gedold fir eng Sprooch ze léieren.
@en You need a lot of patience to learn a language.
@distractor-lu Zäit
@distractor-lu vergiessen
@distractor-en time
@distractor-en forget

@sentence
@lu Ech widderhuele meng Vokabelen all Dag e puer Minutten.
@en I review my vocables every day for a few minutes.
@distractor-lu Woch
@distractor-lu seelen
@distractor-en week
@distractor-en rarely

@sentence
@lu De Google-Iwwersetzer ass net ëmmer exakt.
@en The Google translator is not always accurate.
@distractor-lu Wierderbuch
@distractor-lu praktesch
@distractor-en dictionary
@distractor-en practical

@sentence
@lu Ech verstinn e Text besser wéi eng séier Diskussioun.
@en I understand a text better than a fast discussion.
@distractor-lu Wuert
@distractor-lu lues
@distractor-en word
@distractor-en slow

@sentence
@lu Meng Disziplin ass méi wichteg wéi mäi Niveau.
@en My discipline is more important than my level.
